  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "Under what condition does equality hold in the AM-GM inequality \\((a+b)/2\\ge\\sqrt{ab}\\)?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(a=b\\), and both \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are positive",
    "B": "It is sufficient for \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) to be positive",
    "C": "\\(a+b=1\\)",
    "D": "\\(ab=1\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Assume \\(a,b>0\\). When two positive numbers are equal, their arithmetic mean and geometric mean are equal. To check necessity as well, write\n\\[\n\\frac{a+b}{2}-\\sqrt{ab}\n=\\frac{(\\sqrt a-\\sqrt b)^2}{2}.\n\\]\nThe square vanishes exactly when \\(a=b\\), so under this assumption the answer is A.\n\nThe stem does not specify the domain. For \\(a,b\\ge0\\), the same identity shows that equality holds exactly when \\(a=b\\), including \\(a=b=0\\). Option A excludes this equality case, so its completeness depends on the positive-number convention.",
